+2. **Native cut-based finite occupation detector with explicit minimum destructive footprint.** Recording a cut measures component parity; all six edges around a vertex read occupation. This is already essentially Theorem2 of the current native instrument note, so a fresh isolated-site demonstration is not a worthwhile novelty. A genuinely new version would need a supplied gauge-corrected nondestructive detector with controlled placement/state-action costs, not an ancilla circuit relabeled as physical formation.
