+## Immediate derivation
+
+Let G_v=(-1)^n_v product_{e incident v} tau^x_e=1. After measuring tau^x_e=r and deleting e=(i,j), the remaining state obeys G'_i=G'_j=r and all other G'_v=1. This follows directly from the constraint and gives a record-readable background-charge update. A product of endpoint Majoranas changes precisely these two signs. For two deleted adjacent edges, the associated even Majorana corrections generally anticommute, although the original physical Z projectors commute. Therefore a phase-correct history intertwiner must explicitly account for the composition sign, or work directly with the charged sectors and never pretend the corrections are commuting physical operations. The next proof/control will resolve that point rather than importing a phase-free update.
